\ Stack effect validation error tests

use "testing" ;

"Wrong delta in quotation parameter" test-section
\ The effect says ( n -- n n ) but [ 2 * ] only produces one value
double-wrong: ( n quot: ( n -- n n ) -- n n ) [ call ] ;
[ 5 [ 2 * ] double-wrong ] "caught double-wrong effect error" assert-error

"Wrong delta with concrete effect" test-section
\ The effect says ( a b -- c ) requiring delta -1, but [ drop drop ] has delta -2
add-wrong: ( a b quot: ( a b -- c ) -- c ) [ call ] ;
[ 1 2 [ drop drop ] add-wrong ] "caught add-wrong effect error" assert-error

"Quotation consumes too few values" test-section
\ Effect says ( a b -- ) requiring delta -2, but [ drop ] only has delta -1
consume-wrong: ( a b quot: ( a b -- ) -- ) [ call ] ;
[ 1 2 [ drop ] consume-wrong ] "caught consume-wrong effect error" assert-error

"Unbalanced quotation parameter is not enforced" test-section
\ keep's quot: ( ..a x -- ..b ) has unbalanced row variables, so a
\ wrong-delta quotation is accepted rather than reported
1 [ dup dup ] keep + + + 4 "unbalanced keep accepts over-producing quotation" assert=

"Balanced row variables still enforced" test-section
\ loop's pred: ( ... -- ... ? ) requires delta +1, but [ f f ] has delta +2
[ [ f f ] loop ] "caught wrong-delta loop predicate" assert-error
